From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Apr 2026 16:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra194: rename and enable Tj thermal zone for
 jetson_clocks

NVIDIA's jetson_clocks utility searches thermal zones by name for the
junction temperature sensor using:

    grep -il tj /sys/class/thermal/thermal_zone*/type

For the match to work, the BPMP TJ_MAX thermal zone must be:
  1. registered in sysfs (status = "okay")
  2. named with "tj" in the type string

The upstream DTS defines the zone as "tj-thermal" but with
status = "disabled", which hides it from /sys/class/thermal entirely.

Rename to "Tj-therm" (matching CPU-therm / GPU-therm / AUX-therm
convention from patch 0006) and enable it in the p2972 board DTS.
Without this, jetson_clocks emits "dirname: missing operand" and
"Failed to find policy of Tj thermal zone!" errors.

Signed-off-by: Mateusz Krawczuk <mateusz.krawczuk@cybrixsystems.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194-p2972-0000.dts | 6 ++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi           | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
@@ -3165,7 +3165,7 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};

-		tj-thermal {
+		Tj-therm {
 			thermal-sensors = <&{/bpmp/thermal} TEGRA194_BPMP_THERMAL_ZONE_TJ_MAX>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194-p2972-0000.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194-p2972-0000.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194-p2972-0000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194-p2972-0000.dts
@@ -2498,6 +2498,12 @@
 					type = "critical";
 				};
 			};
 		};
+
+		Tj-therm {
+			polling-delay = <0>;
+			polling-delay-passive = <500>;
+			status = "okay";
+		};
 	};
 };
